s="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI RAYON CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NIIKAWA, KENJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEDA, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TASAKA, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UENISHI, MASAMOTO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATARI, KENJI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KATO OSAMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NIIKAWA KENJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKEDA SATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TASAKA HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UENISHI MASAMOTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WATARI KENJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATO, OSAMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NIIKAWA, KENJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEDA, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TASAKA, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UENISHI, MASAMOTO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATARI, KENJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A hollow yarn membrane module (1), characterized as having a potting agent (2) comprising a cured epoxy resin showing a change of a specimen thereof in mass per surface area ranging from -20 to +20 mg/cm&lt;2&gt; after the immersion of the specimen in a chemical for 6 months, and a housing material (4) comprising a polyolefin showing a change of a specimen thereof in mass per surface area ranging from -20 to +20 mg/cm&lt;2&gt; after the immersion of the specimen in a chemical for 6 months and having a total content of metals of 300 ppm or less; a potting agent for the module; and a method using the module for deaerating a liquid chemical to be used in a semiconductor manufacturing process, in a printer, in a liquid crystal encapsulating process, in a liquid chemical preparing process or the like.  The module is preventive of module leak and can be used for treating a liquid chemical for a long period of time.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Ce module à membrane de fil creux (1) se caractérise par le fait qu'il comporte un agent de remplissage (2), comprenant une résine époxyde durcie dont un échantillon fait montre d'une variation de la masse par surface efficace comprise entre 20 et + 20 mg/cm&lt;2&gt; après immersion dudit échantillon dans une substance chimique pendant six mois, ainsi qu'un matériau d'enveloppe (4), comprenant une polyoléfine dont un échantillon fait montre d'une variation de la masse par surface efficace comprise entre 20 et + 20 mg/cm&lt;2&gt; après immersion dudit échantillon dans une substance chimique pendant six mois, la teneur totale en métaux étant égale ou inférieure à 300 mg/kg. L'invention a également trait à un agent de remplissage destiné à ce module. Elle porte, de surcroît, sur un procédé employant ce module pour désaérer une substance chimique liquide à utiliser dans un processus de fabrication de semi-conducteur, dans une imprimante, dans un processus d'encapsulation de cristaux liquides, dans un processus de préparation de substance chimique liquide ou analogue. Ce module, qui interdit toute fuite, peut être utilisé pour traiter une substance chimique liquide pendant une longue période.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>